# Patterns are **-anchored so they match at any depth: a bare `node_modules` or
# `dist` matches only the context root, which let app/node_modules (~1 GB) and
# app/dist leak into every build.
.venv/
.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.egg-info/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
**/.env
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
**/node_modules/
v2/

# Not inputs to the Python package or the frontend build; keeping them out of
# the build context keeps it small (app/src-tauri is the Rust desktop shell).
app/src-tauri/
app/e2e/
app/playwright-report/
app/test-results/
out/
.hermes/
.audit/
**/*.log
